cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "CD-HIT in Google Colab"
message: "If you use this notebook, please cite it along with CD-HIT itself."
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: Zallot
    given-names: Rémi
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-7317-1578"
    affiliation: "Manchester Metropolitan University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/remizallot/cdhit-colab"
abstract: >-
  A Google Colab notebook that builds CD-HIT from source and runs it in the
  browser, with no local installation. Provided because the CD-HIT web server
  has been unavailable since 2022. All parameters are Colab form fields, so a
  saved notebook records exactly what was run, and each run writes a provenance
  file recording the CD-HIT version, full command line, input checksum and
  timestamp.
keywords:
  - CD-HIT
  - sequence clustering
  - bioinformatics
  - Google Colab
  - reproducibility
